1
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:19,644
No wonder the name sounded familiar.

2
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,772
I was Je Moon-jae too.

3
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,994
I said I'm Je Moon-jae!

4
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:16,034
MOUSETRAP

5
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:19,496
Ms. Han, let me explain it in person.

6
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:22,123
You're the only person I can rely on now.

7
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:26,002
I'll explain everything in person.
Please just hear me out.

8
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:28,129
Say something already!

9
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:30,131
<i>Why won't you say anything?</i>

10
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:33,635
Ms. Han.

11
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:46,272
See?

12
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,483
I told you he'd call again.

13
00:01:57,242 --> 00:02:00,537
Thank you for the drink.
I'm sorry for showing up unannounced.

14
00:02:02,539 --> 00:02:05,750
Still, we should do this again sometime.

15
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:35,530
You have a knife.

16
00:02:37,115 --> 00:02:39,993
Just kill me already, you bastard!

17
00:02:54,841 --> 00:02:56,926
Come on, pick up.

18
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:16,946
You can't park here.

19
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:18,907
It's by the sea. It's dangerous.

20
00:03:19,616 --> 00:03:21,576
Okay, I'll move right away.

21
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:24,120
Have you been drinking?

22
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:26,497
No.

23
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:33,171
Step out for a moment.

24
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:34,422
- Sorry?
- Sir.

25
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:41,346
Wanted vehicle. Urgent.

26
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:43,556
Is this your vehicle?

27
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:46,476
Please step out.

28
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:49,270
I don't understand what's going on.

29
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:51,314
Where the hell is Sun-yong anyway?

30
00:03:57,195 --> 00:04:00,114
What do you mean your name's Moon-jae?

31
00:04:01,532 --> 00:04:03,785
I used to be Je Moon-jae too.

32
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:06,621
You know I'm an orphan.

33
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:12,585
The bastard who dragged me into this
even had my adoption records.

34
00:04:14,796 --> 00:04:16,589
Hey, man.

35
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:19,175
How could you forget your childhood name?

36
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:21,761
You've been after Je Moon-jae
for a while now.

37
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:23,263
Come on.

38
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:26,140
Do you still fucking

39
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:28,977
remember everything clearly
from when you were five?

40
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:32,105
I've got a lot of names.

41
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:35,900
I was adopted and returned three times.

42
00:04:36,484 --> 00:04:39,404
I think my first name was Sang-gyu,
Sang-gu, <i>hogu</i>, or something.

43
00:04:39,487 --> 00:04:40,530
Fucking hell.

44
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:44,117
What was the next one? Hyeon-cheol?

45
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,910
The next one's Park Sun-yong.

46
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:49,163
But my name was Je Moon-jae
when I was five.

47
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:52,625
Damn.

48
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,503
No wonder it sounded fucking familiar.

49
00:04:55,586 --> 00:04:57,046
I said get out of the car.

50
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:59,841
- That's not it.
- I said step out for a moment.

51
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:05,972
Don't move! Damn it.

52
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,434
Get out of the car, you bastard!

53
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:10,518
Get out!

54
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:44,385
But…

55
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:49,390
who are you?

56
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:58,816
Requesting backup.

57
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:01,486
Don't move, you bastard.

58
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:14,082
He said we should rest before we return.

59
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:16,250
Get some sleep.

60
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:39,982
Hey, who is it?

61
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,028
Where is the bastard?

62
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:46,989
He's fine.

63
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,325
That's enough. Bring him out.

64
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:50,243
Yes, sir.

65
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:00,753
Hey.

66
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:01,796
Get in here.

67
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:03,256
Hey, you bastard. Get in here.

68
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:12,640
Where's Noja?

69
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:15,226
I don't know.

70
00:07:16,352 --> 00:07:19,272
Three of our guys died,
you fucking piece of shit!

71
00:07:20,022 --> 00:07:23,067
One of them was expecting a second child,
so he even bought drinks.

72
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:24,986
You son of a bitch.

73
00:07:25,069 --> 00:07:27,822
Why did our guys have to die
over trash like you?

74
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:31,284
Tell me where he is.

75
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:33,077
Noja.

76
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,329
Tell me!

77
00:07:37,623 --> 00:07:38,791
You fucking bastard.

78
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:59,604
HOW DID IT GO?

79
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:01,939
PARK SEUNG-GYU

80
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:12,992
Yeah, I was just about to call you.

81
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:15,244
I got Noja, that bastard,

82
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:16,537
and found that old man.

83
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:22,418
DEOKAM NURSING HOME

84
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:29,842
Hello.

85
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:36,599
<i>Apparently, a bunch of cops</i>
<i>already came by and left.</i>

86
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:37,934
But he has dementia.

87
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:40,019
Doesn't know his own name.
Remembers nothing.

88
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:44,649
So there's nothing to be scared of.

89
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:47,818
That old man, he can't prove anything.

90
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:50,363
So what do we do now?

91
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:52,281
How do I get my money?

92
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:57,328
Fuck. You're right.

93
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:01,207
I didn't even think about that.

94
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:04,377
Okay.

95
00:09:06,337 --> 00:09:07,630
Got it. Okay.

96
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:45,876
Why the fuck is he asking me
to send this shit?

97
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,838
Hey, call the guy at the nursing home.
We've missed something.

98
00:10:17,908 --> 00:10:19,702
Please call that detective.

99
00:10:20,995 --> 00:10:22,496
Then I'll explain everything.

100
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:53,110
Where are you going?

101
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:54,779
The nursing home.

102
00:11:06,624 --> 00:11:07,875
WRITER JE MOON-JAE

103
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:11,796
- Yep.
- <i>Hello, detective. It's Je Moon-jae.</i>

104
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,215
<i>Oh, I know.</i>

105
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:15,549
<i>But what's this about?</i>

106
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:17,176
I heard you found my uncle.

107
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:19,679
Yep.

108
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:21,681
<i>Then that makes things simpler.</i>

109
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:25,142
One simple DNA test
will tell you who the real one is.

110
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:28,145
<i>I just have a feeling you suspect me.</i>

111
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,607
I was thinking the same thing.

112
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:34,485
<i>I'm actually on my way</i>
<i>to the nursing home.</i>

113
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:38,364
Are you sure
you're okay with the DNA test?

114
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:40,783
Of course. Where's my uncle?

115
00:11:40,866 --> 00:11:42,284
I'll head over right now.

116
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,994
I guess you can do that.

117
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:48,541
First, I'll collect your uncle's hair
and a buccal swab, and…

118
00:11:51,001 --> 00:11:52,211
What the hell?

119
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:55,381
For fuck's sake.

120
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:00,261
The patient inhaled a lot of smoke.

121
00:12:11,731 --> 00:12:13,232
For fuck's sake, seriously!

122
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:14,859
Excuse me!

123
00:12:14,942 --> 00:12:17,361
Excuse me. That old man. The elderly man.

124
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:19,280
He should be nearby. Everyone's out.

125
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:20,614
- Really?
- It's so hectic.

126
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:23,576
He should be over there.
He was in the same room as them.

127
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:24,827
- There?
- Yes.

128
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:25,828
Okay.

129
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:56,358
Why are you trembling?
You seemed fine burying your friend there.

130
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:03,532
What

131
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,451
did I do wrong?

132
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:06,994
Huh?

133
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:09,830
If I did something wrong,

134
00:13:11,749 --> 00:13:12,875
I'm sorry.

135
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:15,628
Really.

136
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,005
I'm really sorry!

137
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:19,840
Fuck.

138
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:22,218
Did you even know that I liked you?

139
00:13:23,177 --> 00:13:24,887
I was obsessed with you.

140
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:27,932
I did everything you told me to do
to fucking impress you.

141
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:32,311
I did all your dirty work,
and you don't even fucking know who I am.

142
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:35,898
To someone as mighty as you,
I must've been fucking nobody.

143
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:39,401
And the mighty man got scammed
and lost fucking everything.

144
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:42,613
Was that money yours?

145
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:44,573
Did you make it?

146
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:46,909
I made it, you son of a bitch.

147
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:49,453
I'm sorry.

148
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:53,874
I'm sorry!

149
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:55,543
I'm sorry!

150
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:56,961
I'm sorry.

151
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,921
You didn't even know I gave you work

152
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:01,006
and helped you
when you were broke, did you?

153
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:05,219
Fuck, you did a hell of a lot of bad shit.
Ten times more than me.

154
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:07,388
Ten times? Definitely more. Fuck.

155
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:09,598
Acting all high and mighty,
burying people there.

156
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,392
Did it make you feel like a god?

157
00:14:11,475 --> 00:14:12,393
No.

158
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:14,186
Not at all.

159
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:19,984
You're not the only one who's gonna die.
So don't be too upset.

160
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:43,465
I'll bury every fucking bastard
who knows about my past

161
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:44,717
and leave this country.

162
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,136
Everyone. Even that asshole.

163
00:14:48,804 --> 00:14:50,097
Gotta start a new game.

164
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:55,394
What if I beg for forgiveness?

165
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:57,980
Will you spare me?

166
00:15:11,827 --> 00:15:12,828
Go ahead, then.

167
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,794
I'm sorry.

168
00:15:22,129 --> 00:15:23,339
I was wrong.

169
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:24,965
Please spare me.

170
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:27,343
Never again!

171
00:15:27,843 --> 00:15:29,428
You'll never see me again!

172
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:31,722
Just let me live!

173
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:34,558
Please.

174
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:52,117
- Sir.
- Good night, sir!

175
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,506
Treat yourself to something nice.

176
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:11,387
Thank you, sir!

177
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:14,348
Thank you, sir!

178
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,189
Do you remember?

179
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:25,234
That time you gave me money.

180
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:29,279
I was so fucking scared
'cause I thought I was gonna die.

181
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:31,991
There was a time I wanted to be like you.

182
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:38,038
But I guess I can't anymore.

183
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:43,377
I'm sorry, but it's too late.

184
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:45,754
No!

185
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:47,423
Please!

186
00:16:48,048 --> 00:16:49,216
Spare me!

187
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:51,802
No!

188
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:55,931
No! Just spare my life!

189
00:16:56,015 --> 00:16:57,307
Here's your money back.

190
00:16:59,018 --> 00:16:59,893
Bury him.

191
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:20,414
Aren't you gonna sleep?

192
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:23,917
I'm thinking.

193
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:28,297
About what?

194
00:17:30,215 --> 00:17:31,925
The dog I had when I was a kid.

195
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:36,638
We kept it tied up in the yard
to guard the house.

196
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:40,476
It guarded the house its whole life
until it died of old age.

197
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:42,811
But until it died,

198
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:46,023
it never saw the world beyond that leash.

199
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:49,234
The length of that leash

200
00:17:49,318 --> 00:17:51,236
was its whole world.

201
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:55,783
It must've been dying to get out of there.

202
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:02,581
I don't remember the dog's name,
but as for the leash…

203
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:05,375
I even remember the color of that leash.

204
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:11,715
Maybe it's not that I remember the dog,
but that I remember the leash.

205
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,468
Now that I think of it,

206
00:18:14,551 --> 00:18:17,137
in a way,
that leash was the mark of the dog.

207
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:23,977
Come to think of it, I'm the same too.
Hey, here. Do you see it?

208
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,605
The leash.

209
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:28,941
There's nothing there.

210
00:18:34,029 --> 00:18:36,532
Everyone has memories they want to erase.

211
00:18:37,157 --> 00:18:38,408
But this leash

212
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:42,704
is woven from the memories
you want to erase.

213
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:45,958
Right when you think it's gone,
it grabs you by the throat.

214
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:49,044
In the end,

215
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:51,880
people die by that leash.

216
00:18:54,716 --> 00:18:57,678
Hey, didn't you say
your memories were fading?

217
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:00,806
Don't forget about that leash, you punk,

218
00:19:01,306 --> 00:19:02,724
or you'll…

219
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:07,396
never be able to prove who you are.

220
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:33,005
Je Moon-jae.

221
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:37,634
It's not even a good name.
Why the hell are you fighting over it?

222
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:40,179
The fake one kills someone,

223
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:42,973
frames the other,
and pretends to be the real one?

224
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:47,060
Fuck, who's the real one?
And who's the fake?

225
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:48,395
Huh?

226
00:19:48,478 --> 00:19:49,897
You wanted to see me.

227
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:53,734
Please help me.

228
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:55,944
I've got

229
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:58,530
no one but you.

230
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:00,616
What about Noja?

231
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,039
I don't know.

232
00:20:08,999 --> 00:20:10,209
We lost touch.

233
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,840
There he is.

234
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:46,703
This…

235
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:50,165
They sent this to you.

236
00:20:52,459 --> 00:20:53,752
He died?

237
00:20:57,422 --> 00:21:01,260
You won't even find the body.
That's the cleanest way.

238
00:21:12,062 --> 00:21:14,356
You found your uncle.
Why did you just leave?

239
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:19,820
Why did you just leave?
You bastard. Damn it.

240
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:24,616
He remembered nothing.

241
00:21:27,077 --> 00:21:28,078
There was no point.

242
00:21:28,578 --> 00:21:29,913
DNA.

243
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:36,211
Hey. What's up with your face?

244
00:21:37,629 --> 00:21:39,631
I'm helping you right now.

245
00:21:40,799 --> 00:21:42,843
You should be happy
if you're the real one.

246
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:47,764
Can it…

247
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:48,890
Can it be this easy?

248
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:55,480
After you came by and left…

249
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:59,067
your uncle disappeared.

250
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:02,696
Someone burned down the nursing home
and took it all, even his toothbrush.

251
00:22:02,779 --> 00:22:04,281
In case he left DNA behind.

252
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:15,334
I knew it.

253
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:19,171
It can't be this easy.

254
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:24,009
That's how it's always been so far.

255
00:22:26,636 --> 00:22:30,724
That bastard knows everything about me.
He knows me better than I do.

256
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:32,017
I see.

257
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:35,103
So you don't know anything about this?

258
00:22:35,187 --> 00:22:37,898
I was caught
right after I left the nursing home.

259
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:40,400
I couldn't have moved him.

260
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:42,861
Maybe you've got some bastard helping you.

261
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:50,243
I did.

262
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,417
They're tracking his movements on CCTV.

263
00:22:57,501 --> 00:22:58,668
Your uncle.

264
00:22:58,752 --> 00:23:00,754
You don't even have an alibi.

265
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:02,798
So if we can't find him,

266
00:23:03,715 --> 00:23:05,509
you're the fake one.

267
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:08,011
That's why I asked to see you.

268
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:10,722
I'll tell you everything
that's happened so far.

269
00:23:10,806 --> 00:23:12,474
Who he is,

270
00:23:14,267 --> 00:23:15,602
what happened…

271
00:23:18,063 --> 00:23:19,481
and how it ended up like this.

272
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:23,860
Hey, guys. Listen up.

273
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:27,280
<i>I first met him</i>
<i>at an intercollegiate literature club.</i>

274
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:30,951
We got a new member today.
What? Is he handsome?

275
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:32,828
Introduce yourself.

276
00:23:34,996 --> 00:23:37,958
Hello, I'm the new club member,

277
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,751
Seo Yu-min.

278
00:23:40,252 --> 00:23:41,711
It's very nice to meet you all.

279
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:44,714
Welcome.

280
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:47,926
<i>His first impression wasn't good.</i>

281
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:50,095
<i>How should I put it?</i>

282
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:54,641
<i>He had a ravenous look in his eyes,</i>
<i>like he hadn't eaten in days.</i>

283
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:59,938
<i>The kind of look that makes you think</i>
<i>he'd devour anything.</i>

284
00:24:02,983 --> 00:24:05,193
THE RAT THAT ATE FINGERNAILS

285
00:24:14,911 --> 00:24:16,746
Moon-jae, did you write this?

286
00:24:17,247 --> 00:24:18,915
Why? You think it's good?

287
00:24:19,749 --> 00:24:20,584
It's amazing.

288
00:24:24,337 --> 00:24:25,297
I'm jealous.

289
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:27,591
I wish I could write like you.

290
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:28,508
Man.

291
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:31,094
But I'm too lazy.

292
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:34,431
I still have this much to write,
but I'm getting nowhere.

293
00:24:52,282 --> 00:24:55,827
Actually, there's someone who inspires me.

294
00:24:55,911 --> 00:24:56,912
Who is it?

295
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:07,255
You're gonna wear it out.

296
00:25:08,715 --> 00:25:10,300
<i>The two of us grew close quickly.</i>

297
00:25:10,383 --> 00:25:12,093
This is how people end up alcoholics…

298
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:14,846
<i>It was because of Min-yeong.</i>

299
00:25:15,514 --> 00:25:16,348
Bathroom.

300
00:25:16,431 --> 00:25:17,265
<i>We both…</i>

301
00:25:17,349 --> 00:25:18,391
Get me one more.

302
00:25:18,475 --> 00:25:20,268
<i>…liked Min-yeong.</i>

303
00:25:22,103 --> 00:25:23,939
She can really hold her liquor.

304
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:29,861
What is it?

305
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:34,574
Moon-jae.

306
00:25:37,327 --> 00:25:38,787
What's the deal with you two?

307
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:41,915
What do you mean?
We just go to the same school.

308
00:25:42,749 --> 00:25:43,959
You're sure, right?

309
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:50,840
Whether I'm sure or not,
talking about this is meaningless.

310
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:57,389
Why is it meaningless?

311
00:25:57,472 --> 00:25:59,808
Min-yeong is way out of our league.

312
00:25:59,891 --> 00:26:03,228
Her standards are super high.
We're not even close.

313
00:26:04,688 --> 00:26:06,356
She's definitely out of your league.

314
00:26:09,859 --> 00:26:11,111
But not mine.

315
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:30,463
<i>That summer,</i>

316
00:26:31,256 --> 00:26:33,383
<i>the three of us went on a trip together.</i>

317
00:26:57,741 --> 00:27:00,827
<i>But something happened there.</i>

318
00:28:24,411 --> 00:28:25,495
Min-yeong.

319
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:27,997
I've got something to tell you.
Let's talk.

320
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:31,042
You're drunk. Talk tomorrow.

321
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:33,211
Let go! I just wanna talk to her.

322
00:28:34,713 --> 00:28:36,423
You said you two weren't a thing.

323
00:28:45,849 --> 00:28:47,308
We're dating.

324
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:52,856
We kept it a secret at the club
because he said he'd feel uncomfortable.

325
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,281
Since when?

326
00:29:02,365 --> 00:29:03,783
Before you asked me.

327
00:29:08,621 --> 00:29:11,541
You shouldn't toy with people.

328
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:13,501
Don't you fucking think so?

329
00:29:30,727 --> 00:29:31,853
You are just

330
00:29:32,353 --> 00:29:33,646
jealous of me.

331
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:37,609
You're dying of jealousy
because you want to be me.

332
00:29:37,692 --> 00:29:38,526
Aren't you?

333
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:40,945
Shut up, you son of a bitch!

334
00:29:57,462 --> 00:30:00,507
<i>That was the last time I ever saw him.</i>

335
00:30:01,132 --> 00:30:02,926
<i>I hadn't seen him since that day.</i>

336
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:14,395
Until he came back with my face.

337
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:17,106
You're saying he did all this
just for that?

338
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:18,983
I don't understand either.

339
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:20,693
Is this really worth all this?

340
00:30:26,449 --> 00:30:29,953
He went ballistic,
like someone took what was his.

341
00:30:32,163 --> 00:30:36,042
Does it make any sense that he changed
his face to yours and killed that girl

342
00:30:36,125 --> 00:30:37,460
after all this time?

343
00:30:38,253 --> 00:30:40,547
There must be more to it, you bastard.

344
00:30:42,757 --> 00:30:43,758
There is.

345
00:30:44,717 --> 00:30:46,386
Something I didn't know about.

346
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:49,764
I heard about this later,

347
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:53,893
but that bastard
wasn't even a university student.

348
00:30:54,644 --> 00:30:56,729
He was pretending to be one
from the start.

349
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:58,731
Creepy, isn't it?

350
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:01,150
What happened between you and that girl?

351
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:04,404
Well,

352
00:31:05,655 --> 00:31:06,823
it just fizzled out.

353
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:11,286
I heard she met someone later
and lived with him.

354
00:31:13,454 --> 00:31:15,123
We shouldn't have gone on that trip.

355
00:31:15,206 --> 00:31:17,667
That trip's what caused all this mess.

356
00:31:24,215 --> 00:31:25,633
Tell me about your parents.

357
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:30,013
Prove that you're the real one.

358
00:31:30,096 --> 00:31:32,140
Something the fake one wouldn't know.

359
00:31:44,235 --> 00:31:45,236
<i>My mom</i>

360
00:31:46,279 --> 00:31:48,615
<i>had some mental issues.</i>

361
00:31:49,949 --> 00:31:51,868
<i>I don't know why,</i>

362
00:31:52,368 --> 00:31:56,372
<i>but ever since I was born,</i>
<i>our home was never like other families'.</i>

363
00:32:57,392 --> 00:32:59,602
<i>My father said I took after my mom.</i>

364
00:33:00,103 --> 00:33:02,647
<i>Maybe that's why I inherited</i>
<i>her illness too.</i>

365
00:33:06,526 --> 00:33:09,070
<i>After that,</i>
<i>I could feel myself losing my mind.</i>

366
00:33:09,654 --> 00:33:11,489
I couldn't live without my meds.

367
00:33:11,572 --> 00:33:12,949
I'm still like that now.

368
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:17,453
Maybe it's the meds,
but my old memories are fading.

369
00:33:18,705 --> 00:33:21,290
Once I completely forget who I am,

370
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:24,168
he will become the real one, right?

371
00:33:25,128 --> 00:33:26,504
The vanity in the bedroom.

372
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:29,882
What did it look like?

373
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:34,345
It was just…

374
00:33:36,556 --> 00:33:38,099
a regular vanity.

375
00:33:39,642 --> 00:33:40,476
Black.

376
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:44,230
A black one.

377
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:56,617
<i>With no patterns.</i>

378
00:33:57,243 --> 00:33:59,746
<i>Not even shiny. Just black.</i>

379
00:34:03,499 --> 00:34:04,417
<i>A square-shaped one.</i>

380
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:06,044
A rectangle.

381
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:08,504
How did you know?

382
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:12,091
We had one like that at home too.

383
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:17,722
Now I fucking get it.

384
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:22,935
My role was to put you in jail.

385
00:34:31,778 --> 00:34:34,447
For one, you don't have much time.
And no alibi either.

386
00:34:34,530 --> 00:34:37,283
Everything you have
is evidence against you.

387
00:34:37,366 --> 00:34:40,161
If you get indicted like this,
you're done.

388
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:44,749
If you have anything more to add,
tell me now.

389
00:34:44,832 --> 00:34:47,210
Anything that proves you're the real one.

390
00:34:48,044 --> 00:34:48,878
All of it.

391
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:36,217
Yes, that property damage case.
The one with the smashed car.

392
00:35:36,300 --> 00:35:39,387
CONSTRUCTION EQUIPMENT PARTS DEALER

393
00:35:39,470 --> 00:35:41,139
Sir, have a good one.

394
00:35:41,889 --> 00:35:44,392
- So you didn't see anything?
- No, I didn't.

395
00:35:44,475 --> 00:35:45,434
Thank you.

396
00:35:52,900 --> 00:35:56,696
I mean, why are we here looking for CCTVs?

397
00:35:56,779 --> 00:35:59,157
How did this become our case?

398
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:01,450
The one who knows
is at the police station.

399
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:05,163
I mean, why's he at another station?

400
00:36:05,246 --> 00:36:06,914
Major Crimes called him.

401
00:36:07,790 --> 00:36:09,500
Seriously.

402
00:36:10,501 --> 00:36:11,419
Hello?

403
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:14,797
What? Why?

404
00:36:16,799 --> 00:36:17,633
What? Well…

405
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:20,595
Find anything?

406
00:36:20,678 --> 00:36:21,888
Nothing, of course.

407
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,598
I mean, you have to tell me why…

408
00:36:25,099 --> 00:36:27,602
Who is it? Is it Sun-yong?

409
00:36:27,685 --> 00:36:29,729
- Let me talk to that bastard.
- He hung up.

410
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:31,105
- What?
- Wait, so…

411
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:32,523
What did the captain say?

412
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:35,484
He said to leave Chang-u here.

413
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:38,196
- He wants the rest of us at the station.
- Me?

414
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:39,780
Why?

415
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:43,326
He said he'll tell us when we're there.

416
00:36:43,409 --> 00:36:44,744
That damn bastard.

417
00:36:50,499 --> 00:36:54,587
INTERROGATION ROOM 1

418
00:36:55,963 --> 00:36:57,131
Let's take a break.

419
00:36:57,798 --> 00:36:59,759
We should have him change clothes too.

420
00:37:00,384 --> 00:37:01,469
Let's call for backup.

421
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:04,430
We have to find Noja's body
or something to close this case.

422
00:37:04,513 --> 00:37:06,682
Seung-gyu and his men are probably nearby.

423
00:37:06,766 --> 00:37:09,977
If we go back to Seoul now,
we won't get anything out of this.

424
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:23,199
I mean, but why did he ask for you? Huh?

425
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:25,159
He didn't even say anything useful.

426
00:37:25,243 --> 00:37:26,786
I guess I make people comfortable.

427
00:37:26,869 --> 00:37:28,829
Unlike detectives who beat people.

428
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:31,666
Maybe that wasn't funny.

429
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:36,629
You know how our job is.
You get close chasing people around.

430
00:37:36,712 --> 00:37:40,091
He started falling apart
after finding out Noja was dead.

431
00:37:40,174 --> 00:37:43,803
He's slowly starting to talk,
so I'll try to dig deeper.

432
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:45,221
Go grab lunch.

433
00:37:45,304 --> 00:37:47,348
Just order us two bowls of <i>gukbap</i>.

434
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:52,103
Let's just go eat.

435
00:37:54,772 --> 00:37:55,606
Let's go.

436
00:37:57,858 --> 00:37:59,735
All right, enjoy your lunch!

437
00:38:21,882 --> 00:38:22,717
Where's my uncle?

438
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:24,969
Come with me.

439
00:38:43,237 --> 00:38:49,618
INTERROGATION ROOM 2

440
00:38:57,960 --> 00:38:58,919
Where's my uncle?

441
00:39:00,671 --> 00:39:03,549
You didn't even remember him.
Desperate to see him now?

442
00:39:04,800 --> 00:39:08,471
I guess people really are drawn
to the same blood.

443
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:11,849
The CSI team's coming to take your DNA.

444
00:39:11,932 --> 00:39:14,018
So sit down and wait a bit.

445
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:16,854
Should I get you something to drink?

446
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:25,029
Then wait here for a moment.

447
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:59,688
"Just smuggle him out for now"?
What's going on here?

448
00:40:00,815 --> 00:40:03,818
Sir, the whole team's necks
are on the line.

449
00:40:03,901 --> 00:40:05,945
You might even lose your pension.

450
00:40:07,113 --> 00:40:08,447
To hell with it!

451
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:09,782
Let's just do it.

452
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:11,283
- Right on.
- Yeah.

453
00:40:12,576 --> 00:40:15,871
Hey, you heard that, right?
We're all risking our necks for this.

454
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:18,666
- Hurry up, punk.
- Got it? Just follow us quietly.

455
00:40:34,557 --> 00:40:36,559
HAN CHANG-U:
FOUND THE SUSPECT VEHICLE.

456
00:40:36,642 --> 00:40:39,103
TRACED ITS MOVEMENTS.
WHERE IS EVERYONE ANYWAY?

457
00:40:39,854 --> 00:40:41,188
Sir!

458
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:42,356
Sir, over here.

459
00:40:44,066 --> 00:40:45,067
Here.

460
00:40:46,944 --> 00:40:48,112
Go in. Here.

461
00:40:55,536 --> 00:40:56,454
Yes, here.

462
00:40:58,205 --> 00:40:59,874
You haven't eaten, right?

463
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:02,251
Well, I felt bad eating by myself.

464
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:04,879
Let's eat together, all right?

465
00:41:07,089 --> 00:41:08,048
Sir, how much is it?

466
00:41:16,015 --> 00:41:17,933
Wait. I'm not sure I have any coins.

467
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:22,313
You wanted coffee, right?

468
00:41:22,396 --> 00:41:23,439
Yes.

469
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:27,318
Oh man.

470
00:41:37,411 --> 00:41:38,245
Hey, you bastard.

471
00:41:39,830 --> 00:41:43,417
He traced the uncle's movements.
We have to find him first.

472
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:44,752
<i>Hurry up and go.</i>

473
00:41:44,835 --> 00:41:46,295
Hey, you bastard.

474
00:41:46,378 --> 00:41:47,713
<i>Oh, and</i>

475
00:41:47,796 --> 00:41:49,924
I found out
who the woman in the river was.

476
00:41:50,007 --> 00:41:52,009
I'll join you
after checking one more thing.

477
00:41:52,092 --> 00:41:53,177
<i>Go as fast as you can.</i>

478
00:41:53,260 --> 00:41:54,094
Check what?

479
00:41:54,178 --> 00:41:56,764
The evidence that the bastard
is the real one.

480
00:42:00,476 --> 00:42:01,352
What did he say?

481
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:04,396
No fucking idea.

482
00:42:05,814 --> 00:42:07,274
He said this one's the real one.

483
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:24,083
It wasn't bad, right?

484
00:42:24,166 --> 00:42:26,293
I actually liked the other place better.

485
00:42:30,631 --> 00:42:31,757
I'm so tired.

486
00:42:39,265 --> 00:42:40,766
You should see this, sir.

487
00:42:44,937 --> 00:42:46,063
What the hell?

488
00:42:46,146 --> 00:42:48,357
Why did he change the interrogation room?

489
00:43:12,965 --> 00:43:14,008
He said he lost him.

490
00:43:14,508 --> 00:43:16,927
He lost an old man
who was barely even alive?

491
00:43:17,761 --> 00:43:20,139
Goddamn it. Fucking bastards.

492
00:43:22,766 --> 00:43:23,934
Which mountain is that?

493
00:43:25,311 --> 00:43:26,145
What do we do?

494
00:43:26,228 --> 00:43:29,315
What do you think? Turn the car around.
You fucking dumbasses!

495
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:31,150
Fuck.

496
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:49,209
PARK SEUNG-GYU

497
00:43:58,719 --> 00:43:59,887
<i>Hey, it's me.</i>

498
00:44:00,888 --> 00:44:01,972
<i>He said he lost him.</i>

499
00:44:02,598 --> 00:44:05,267
<i>I'll take care of it. Don't worry.</i>

500
00:44:08,228 --> 00:44:09,730
Fucking idiots.

501
00:44:13,692 --> 00:44:16,695
Hey! That bastard's looking at a phone!

502
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:18,280
Where did he get it? Hey!

503
00:44:24,203 --> 00:44:25,120
Who are you?

504
00:44:27,831 --> 00:44:28,666
Me?

505
00:44:31,126 --> 00:44:33,170
I'm Je Moon-jae.

506
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:36,799
Je Moon-jae, the complainant and victim!

507
00:44:49,728 --> 00:44:50,562
Isn't that it?

508
00:44:50,646 --> 00:44:52,773
Yeah, that's it. 1917.

509
00:44:52,856 --> 00:44:55,442
Man, how are we supposed to find him here?

510
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:57,986
Even the whole Mobile Police Unit
would take a month.

511
00:44:58,070 --> 00:45:00,322
We can't even use drones.
The forest's too dense.

512
00:45:02,241 --> 00:45:06,120
If he went up some remote mountain,
he'd have left traces unless he's a ghost.

513
00:45:06,203 --> 00:45:08,539
Quit whining and follow me, punk.
Time is precious.

514
00:45:09,206 --> 00:45:10,457
- Get your gear.
- Okay.

515
00:45:12,543 --> 00:45:13,836
What about him?

516
00:45:16,797 --> 00:45:19,508
Hey, cuff him to the steering wheel.

517
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:21,927
Oh, I'll come with you and help.

518
00:45:24,596 --> 00:45:26,724
My uncle is the only evidence.

519
00:45:49,955 --> 00:45:52,666
<i>I'm with the police.</i>
<i>I'd like to check some school records.</i>

520
00:45:57,671 --> 00:45:58,672
He's not here.

521
00:45:58,756 --> 00:46:00,007
STUDENT RECORD
SO MIN-YEONG

522
00:46:00,090 --> 00:46:01,759
What are you talking about? No way.

523
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:04,386
We never had a student by that name.

524
00:46:04,470 --> 00:46:06,221
Could it have been another school?

525
00:46:06,930 --> 00:46:08,599
No. It's definitely this school.

526
00:46:08,682 --> 00:46:10,976
Please check again.

527
00:46:13,353 --> 00:46:16,565
The student records from the '70s on
have all been computerized.

528
00:46:16,648 --> 00:46:18,859
He wouldn't be from the '60s, right?

529
00:46:18,942 --> 00:46:23,238
Even students who dropped out are in here.
If he's not here, he never attended.

530
00:46:26,784 --> 00:46:28,076
Seo Yu-min.

531
00:46:29,912 --> 00:46:32,581
Can you try searching Seo Yu-min?

532
00:46:32,664 --> 00:46:33,916
Seo Yu-min?

533
00:46:35,209 --> 00:46:38,378
Oh, that name's here.
Korean Language and Literature.

534
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:41,298
He and the girl from that record
were in the same major.

535
00:46:42,925 --> 00:46:44,384
<i>I heard about this later,</i>

536
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:45,677
<i>but that bastard</i>

537
00:46:46,261 --> 00:46:47,763
wasn't even a university student.

538
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:50,599
<i>He was pretending to be one</i>
<i>from the start.</i>

539
00:46:50,682 --> 00:46:51,642
<i>Creepy, isn't it?</i>

540
00:46:52,142 --> 00:46:54,311
<i>It was just a regular vanity. Damn it.</i>

541
00:46:54,394 --> 00:46:55,896
<i>I said it first.</i>

542
00:46:56,647 --> 00:46:58,774
<i>Before I even asked him</i>
<i>what it looked like.</i>

543
00:47:00,818 --> 00:47:02,069
Fuck.

544
00:47:25,217 --> 00:47:26,426
Yes, sir.

545
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:29,346
I can't hear you. Say that again.

546
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:31,723
We're following the trail.

547
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:33,517
What? Who?

548
00:47:34,601 --> 00:47:37,437
Yeah, he came with us.
He said he wanted to help.

549
00:47:39,857 --> 00:47:40,691
Huh?

550
00:47:43,068 --> 00:47:43,902
Where did he go?

551
00:47:46,405 --> 00:47:47,614
Sir!

552
00:47:48,115 --> 00:47:49,575
Yeah? What is it?

553
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:52,411
What is it?

554
00:47:54,371 --> 00:47:55,330
What?

555
00:47:55,414 --> 00:47:56,498
Here…

556
00:47:56,582 --> 00:47:58,125
Where's Je Moon-jae?

557
00:47:58,208 --> 00:47:59,501
Goddamn it.

558
00:48:00,168 --> 00:48:01,712
- Where is he?
- He's gone.

559
00:48:01,795 --> 00:48:03,922
- What?
- This is bullshit. Seriously.

560
00:48:19,354 --> 00:48:20,606
<i>They won't find my uncle.</i>

561
00:48:21,732 --> 00:48:25,569
<i>He was buried somewhere on this mountain,</i>
<i>gone forever, just like Noja.</i>

562
00:48:26,695 --> 00:48:30,032
<i>I have to catch the Rat.</i>
<i>That's the only way.</i>

563
00:48:31,491 --> 00:48:34,036
<i>How am I supposed to prove I'm human?</i>

564
00:48:34,578 --> 00:48:35,704
<i>No.</i>

565
00:48:35,787 --> 00:48:36,997
<i>Even if I were the Rat,</i>

566
00:48:37,748 --> 00:48:39,875
<i>how could I ever admit it?</i>

567
00:53:14,566 --> 00:53:17,485
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
